  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Meant for tanks under about 350 litres.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Works in both freshwater and marine tanks.",
      "source": 9
    },
    {
      "fact": "For the Thermo version, the reviewer found the 200 W built-in heater too weak for large tanks and suggests also running a backup heater.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "The reviewer thinks the many removable parts may make it a poor pick for beginners.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "You can fit a heating element to the plain BioMaster 350 later on.",
      "source": 9
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Has a built-in pump on top for priming; in one test it took about 5–6 presses to start the siphon, the canister filled in under a minute and air cleared in 10–15 seconds.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "The EasyClean pre-filter comes out on its own, so you can clean it often without opening the main media; this protects the main filter wool.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Flow can be adjusted at several points on the filter.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Handle safety locks and check valves in the hose connections help prevent spills when you disconnect it.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "When servicing, clean the pre-filter sponges, the spray bar and the underside of the head; some parts must be unlocked in a set order.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "Oase advises taking out and cleaning the impeller, and replacing it if it is worn or damaged.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "Ships with basic media only; you can swap in your own media.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "If you buy online in Vietnam, film the unboxing to back up any warranty claim.",
      "source": 3
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "The most common complaint is an impeller hum that starts after a few months; some owners fixed it by adding a soft spacer at the impeller support.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 350 and larger sizes are reported to run slightly louder than the 250, at roughly 41–44 dB measured close to the head; other owners still call it quieter than Eheim.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "Biofilm on the impeller and its housing can make it noisier.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "Leaks mostly show up right after maintenance; one long-term owner keeps a spare inlet/outlet adapter.",
      "source": 6
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some users report trouble with priming and trapped air.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "In one test, measured flow was far below the rating: about 138 gph with media against 300 gph claimed.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "The Thermo version has four seal points, which means more places that could leak.",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "BioMaster 2 is a redesign that a VN shop says has more than 25% higher flow, and it costs more (8.91 million VND vs about 6.2–7.44 million for the first version).",
      "source": 3
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
